      "module": "lesen",
      "title": "The Benefits of Breakfast",
      "text": "Many people believe that breakfast is the most important meal of the day. Research suggests that eating a healthy breakfast can (1) ______ your energy levels and help you focus better at school or work. However, skipping this meal is a common habit for those who are in a rush. Instead of grabbing a sugary snack, it is (2) ______ to choose something nutritious like porridge or fruit. These foods provide the vitamins your body needs to (3) ______ properly throughout the morning. Some people find it difficult to eat early, but even a small portion can make a big (4) ______. If you are not hungry, try drinking a smoothie (5) ______ of eating a full meal. Developing these simple habits will (6) ______ you feel much healthier and more alert every single day.",
